+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+The desk has to see at a glance what can still be rented for a given period. Today the only way to find out is to try `book` on each item and catch the error.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `availability({ start, end, kind? })` to the rental service. It returns the sorted ids of the equipment, of the given kind or of any kind when none is given, that is free for the whole period.
+- The period follows the existing whole-day rules; an invalid period or an unknown `kind` is rejected.
+- The "exposes `addEquipment`, `quote` and `book` only" requirement is updated, as it would otherwise contradict the new operation. Cancellation is still not offered.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `equipment-rental`: adds an availability requirement and updates the operations listed in the cancellation-policy requirement.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: new method on `RentalService` and its implementation.
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: new tests.
+- No new dependency, no change to `quote` or `book`.
